    "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nThe Terraform generator, exact-path verifier and artifact gate still use separate implementations from the accepted PowerShell foundation. This change ports the shared implementation from [PSStyleGuide PR234](https://github.com/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/pull/234), accepted at `98177628b7bc02c646724bfc8aa0fd73fed0cd24` (tree `fd66ed6c5b94d8c012a0aa06c8d30f2ae16746c6`). Terraform keeps its own language descriptors and current recovery checks.\n\nThe generator builds complete payloads before publication and uses common versioned result contracts. The artifact gate checks the actual Terraform semantic child, its native status and its integrity effects before generation. It retains the first resolved Node executable, bounded child wait, independent output allowlist, exact-path verification and final byte checks. The shared tests retain all 16 Terraform semantic modes and the candidate/final identity and primary-error/cleanup controls accepted in PR234.\n\nThe build now runs the actual generator suite twice on Windows PowerShell 5.1, Windows PowerShell 7 and native-ext4 Linux PowerShell 7. Verification requires successful results from all three jobs for the same revision before artifact publication. Both Linux acquisition callers retain early Git-selector refusal and checked byte configuration. The finite workflow policy, mutation cases and instruction-maintenance classifier recognize these consumers.\n\n## Scope and retained decisions\n\nExactly 12 files under `.github/workflows` change. The shared source bytes are identical to the accepted PowerShell source except for these bounded differences:\n\n- Generator: one marked Terraform language descriptor.\n- Artifact gate: a separate Terraform descriptor with `TerraformRecovery` semantics.\n- CI-helper tests: eight exact repository identity substitutions.\n- Build: ten repository identity substitutions, the existing Terraform verifier role `verify` at two sites, and the Terraform scoped output path.\n- Script index: one common harness row is added; the current Terraform semantic entry, verifier role and T1 provenance link remain.\n\nThe independent Terraform workflow-policy contract, actual `Test-StateRecoveryExamples.mjs`, guides, four generated documents, dependencies and other 67 existing tracked files retain their accepted bytes. The source's D1/D2/D3/D4 selections and R2\u2013R11 dispositions apply to the identical shared regions; this mechanical transfer introduces no new product design choice. The accepted source review and this PR's own validation remain separate evidence.\n\nThis preserves the current filesystem threat-model limits. The identity controls and injected mutation tests do not establish protection against every hostile competing writer. [PS issue155](https://github.com/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/issues/155) remains open. Generator platform proof does not count as recovery-harness platform proof or a human recovery gate.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe candidate is commit `6c0c987799425b60c0e7b76650aa5ec7946811e2`, based on Terraform main `e21b74fe0b56551008f78f9f2946cd2a0f9c19ce`, with tree `ced4bb594a121b6c1ead983242ce2967032edd96`.\n\n- Four PowerShell files: zero parser errors and zero PSScriptAnalyzer 1.24.0 warnings/errors.\n- Actual local Windows PowerShell 7.6.5 generator suite: 156 assertions passed twice.\n- Isolated local Linux PowerShell 7.6.3 generator suite: 156 assertions passed twice in `Current` mode. This is not the required hosted native-ext4 cell.\n- Actual Terraform generation on Linux: two `NoChange` results; all four accepted output byte sequences remain identical.\n- Actual Linux Terraform recovery examples: passed.\n- Seven Node 24.18.1 suites: 567 tests passed, zero failures/cancellations/skips.\n- Root raw comparison: all 12 postimages match the selected source port, all 67 unchanged files retain accepted bytes, and all 1,910 dependency files match their verified catalog.\n\nAll 11 repository hooks and the final source/dependency/ref/config guard passed on the final candidate. Normal commit hooks, all four actual committed endpoint checks (accepted maintenance classification, metadata finalization, metadata classification and proposed policy) and the current ordinary two-root dependency audit passed. Independent candidate quality found no material defect. Final published head/base/body binding, this PR's remote reviews, hosted Windows5.1/Windows7/native-ext4Linux7 results and clean-commit artifact gate remain required. Local Windows5.1 execution is restricted and was not bypassed.\n\nAfter normal reviewed landing and landed validation, compare the actual merged Terraform bytes and coupled contracts back to current PowerShell main. This PR alone does not declare full paired-plan completion.\n",
    "changed_files": 12
  },
